and hippocampus-dependent memory in inbred mice</article-title><source>Learn Mem</source><year>2000</year><volume>7</volume><fpage>170</fpage><lpage>179</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">10837506</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1101/lm.7.3.170</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B24"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Kolesnikov</surname><given-names>Y</given-names></name><name><surname>Jain</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><name><surname>Wilson</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name><name><surname>Pasternak</surname><given-names>GW</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Lack of morphine and enkephalin tolerance in 129/SvEv mice: evidence for a NMDA receptor defect</article-title><source>J Pharmacol Exp Ther</source><year>1998</year><volume>284</volume><fpage>455</fpage><lpage>459</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">9454784</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B25"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Bardoni</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Excitatory synaptic transmission in neonatal dorsal horn: NMDA and ATP receptors</article-title><source>News Physiol Sci</source><year>2001</year><volume>16</volume><fpage>95</fpage><lpage>100</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">11390958</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B26"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Beggs</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><name><surname>Torsney</surname><given-names>C</given-names></name><name><surname>Drew</surname><given-names>LJ</given-names></name><name><surname>Fitzgerald</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>The postnatal reorganization of primary afferent input and dorsal horn cell receptive fields in the rat spinal cord is an activity-dependent process</article-title><source>Eur J Neurosci</source><year>2002</year><volume>16</volume><fpage>1249</fpage><lpage>1258</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">12405985</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1046/j.1460-9568.2002.02185.x</pub-id></citation></ref></ref-list></back></article>